      "text": "To solve the system of equations\n\\[\n3x - 5y = -11 \\quad \\text{(1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n7x + 2y = -12 \\quad \\text{(2)}\n\\]\nwe can use the method of elimination.\n\nFirst, we will multiply equation (1) by 2 and equation (2) by 5 to eliminate the \\(y\\) terms. \n\nMultiplying equation (1) by 2:\n\\[\n2(3x - 5y) = 2(-11) \\implies 6x - 10y = -22 \\quad \\text{(3)}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying equation (2) by 5:\n\\[\n5(7x + 2y) = 5(-12) \\implies 35x + 10y = -60 \\quad \\text{(4)}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add equation (3) and equation (4):\n\\[\n(6x - 10y) + (35x + 10y) = -22 + (-60)\n\\]\n\\[\n6x + 35x = -82\n\\]\n\\[\n41x = -82\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{82}{41} = -2\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(x = -2\\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(y\\). We will use equation (1):\n\\[\n3(-2) - 5y = -11\n\\]\n\\[\n-6 - 5y = -11\n\\]\n\\[\n-5y = -11 + 6\n\\]\n\\[\n-5y = -5\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\\[\n(x, y) = (-2, 1)\n\\]\n\nTo verify this solution using Python, let's implement the steps in code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the symbols\nx, y = symbols('x y')\n\n# Define the equations\neq1 = Eq(3*x - 5*y, -11)\neq2 = Eq(7*x + 2*y, -12)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (x, y))\n\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{x: -2, y: 1}\n```\nThe solution to the system of equations is:\n\\[\n(x, y) = \\boxed{(-2, 1)}\n\\]",
