      "text": "We can multiply the second equation by $2$ to make the coefficient of $y$ in the second equation equal to $-10:$ $$\\begin{align*}\n2(7x+2y) &= 2(-12)\\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad 14x + 4y &= -24\\qquad\\checkmark\\\\\n3x-5y&=-11\\qquad\\checkmark\n\\end{align*}$$\nNext, we can add the equations together to eliminate $y.$ $$\\begin{align*}\n3x-5y + 14x+4y &= -11+(-24)\\\\\n17x &= -35\\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad x &= \\boxed{-\\frac{35}{17}}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThen we can substitute this value of $x$ back into one of the equations to solve for $y.$ $$\\begin{align*}\n3x-5y&=-11\\\\\n3\\left(-\\frac{35}{17}\\right)-5y&=-11\\\\\n-\\frac{105}{17} - 5y &= -11\\\\\n-\\frac{105}{17} + 5y &= -11\\\\\n-5y &= -\\frac{138}{17}\\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad y &= \\boxed{\\frac{138}{85}}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus, the values of $x$ and $y$ that satisfy the system of equations is $\\boxed{(-\\frac{35}{17},\\frac{138}{85})}$.The answer is: (-\\frac{35}{17},\\frac{138}{85})",
